From 52040081a7dfb3ebbecbc000b59a7b2511000b65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 02:14:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [rh2-integration] structured G1 acceptance events +
 integration-tree identity assertion

rh2 pre-rental blockers B1/B2/B3 (miles side):

- new miles/utils/rh2_event_log.py: append-only jsonl event log gated by
  MILES_RH2_EVENT_DIR (no-op when unset), plus miles source-tree digest and
  per-actor identity assertion pinned by RH2_EXPECTED_MILES_TREE_DIGEST.
- train_one_step: emit per-optimizer-step 'train_step' events carrying the
  independent facts the acceptance judge needs: optimizer_step_applied (true
  only when optimizer.step() really ran; the NORMAL enum alone is not proof),
  Adam/scheduler progress counters before/after, grad_norm, duration, and the
  aggregated dis_* token-accounting metrics (aggregation hoisted so skipped
  steps also report; collective stays rank-aligned).
- train(): emit 'train_step_consumed' with each DP rank's contiguous per-step
  sample-index slice (queue exactly-once + positive-control consumption).
- actor: 'train_rollout' carries the trainer-side current weight version at
  consumption time (behavior weight_versions must not stand in for it);
  'logprob_compare' reports same-version |current-behavior| per sample over
  the support-renormalized recomputed log_probs; 'weight_update' records
  version before/after and duration on rank 0.
- rollout_manager.generate: 'rollout_workers' (stable engine identity set)
  and per-group 'rollout_group' sample identity/reward/behavior-version/
  routing-tape-digest evidence; eval path emits 'eval_smoke'.
- fully-async data buffer: 'group_filtered' rejection evidence (aborted /
  dynamic-filter drops), proving zero-variance groups never trained.
- train_async driver: 'weight_publish' / 'weight_publish_skipped' mark the
  publish gate decision; driver + every actor kind assert tree identity at
  startup and stop on mismatch.

